1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Excerpts taken from document written by Ingeborg (Hallingby) Rasch to establish the fact that Frithjof Rasch and Fred A. are the same person*
2 CONT
2 CONT Frithjof Rasch lived in Norway for 6 years before leaving for America on the boat Tingvalla with his mother Ingeborg (Hallingby) Rasch and his two brothers Halvor Hjaerdahl and Hans Adolph. Hans died after the family arrived in Re
2 CONC dwing MN.  They joined Alfred Christian Michael Rasch, son of Hans Adolph and Dora who were then owners of Hoff estate at Honefos, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT They lived in MN for about 5 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1885 the family moved to Portland OR, where another son, Grover was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Frithjof entered high school he registered as Fred A. Rasch and from then on adopted and retained that name.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended Stanford University in Palo Alto California where he was secretary of the Alpha Literary Society, President of the Gymnasium Club, a member of the fencing Club, organizer of the Pedestrian Club, and a member of the Exe
2 CONC cutive Committe of the student body.
2 CONT
2 CONT All of which are recorded in Volume III of the Stanford Quad 1897. He was president of the Stanford Club of Portland OR in 1903 and a director of the club for five years in Washington DC.
