0 @N6000000005016831440@ NOTE http://piercebios.tripod.com/surnamesH.htm
1 CONT HEYERDAHL, Nils worked in the neighborhood of his father's home for several years. In May 1878, he secured a situation as apprentice in the George Fortune mill at River Falls, Wis., where he has remained until the present time, no
1 CONC w holding the position he has of head miller. He was married October 28,, 1886, to Otella Haloorson, of River Falls. He has no children, but has adopted his niece Hilda, the daughter of his oldest sister, Elizabeth. Hilda lives wi
1 CONC th her foster parents and attends the public schools. Nils Heyerdahl is a member of the Ezekiel Lutheran church, of River Falls, having been trustee of that church for three terms of three years each, stills serving in that capaci
1 CONC ty. He is a member of Kinnickinnic lodge, No. 30, United Foresters, of River Falls, and Glen Colony Lodge of the Beavers, of River Falls. He is independent in politics and is highly thought of as progressive, respected and well in
1 CONC formed gentleman. Reference: Taken from "History of the St. Croix Valley", published in 1909
