0 @N6000000007329285640@ NOTE [NYMARGIT.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Andersʼ younger brothers farmed at Lynes, while Anders as second son,
1 CONT didnʼt start farming his own farm before he was 30 years old . Nobody
1 CONT knows the reason for this arrangement. One can only guess that Anders,
1 CONT for unknown reasons, was unable to loosen his brothers and sisters to
1 CONT get his allodium. In such cases, it was very common that a young man
1 CONT looked around for an available  widow. In the year 1659, Anders found
1 CONT a such one, at the farm Southern Doknes. We donʼt know any children in
1 CONT this marriage, but one, OLE. In his second marriage with Birgithe
1 CONT Christophersdaughter Ingelsrud from Nannestad municipality. We don't
1 CONT know if they had children- February 1685 Anders and his son Ole
1 CONT purchased  Fremming farm. However Anders continued his farming at
1 CONT Doknes till 1701, when he moved to Fremming and became Oleʼs fellow
1 CONT farmer there. "Slekten Ørbø" (1983) by Ola Ljødal
0 @N6000000007329285509@ NOTE [NYMARGIT.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT By a deed of 1765, Anders bought half of the Upper Ulvin farm from her
1 CONT mother and stepfather, i.e. half of the houses and the land for 180
1 CONT daler. From then on this farm was called Lower Ulvin. Anders married
1 CONT Karen Jensdaughter, who died in 1776. Children: Halvor, Ole, Martha.
1 CONT The son Halvor moved to Baalsrud in Feiring, and got many descendants.
